<title>ITALY: Italian crude imports up 1.4 pct in Jan-Nov 1996.</title>
<headline>Italian crude imports up 1.4 pct in Jan-Nov 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian imports of crude oil amounted to 67.4 million tonnes in the first 11 months of 1996, up 1.4 percent from the same period in 1995, industry association Unione Petrolifera said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Libya accounted for 32.1 percent of imports, Iran 17.6 percent, Saudi Arabia 14.3 percent and the former Soviet Union 12.4 percent.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
